\title{PhysioNetPhysiology: Network Physiology for the Physio ecosystem}
\description{
Dynamic-interaction analysis of coupled physiological systems. The package
centres on \strong{Time Delay Stability (TDS)} — a method that detects stable
temporal couplings between signals by tracking, over sliding windows, the lag
that maximises their cross-correlation and rewarding periods where that lag
stays put. Stable couplings become links in an \emph{organ-interaction network}
whose edges are significance-tested against phase-randomised surrogates, and
the package quantifies how such networks \strong{reconfigure across physiological
states} (wake / sleep stages, rest / task, ...).
}
\details{
Core entry points:
\itemize{
\item \code{\link[=timeDelayStability]{timeDelayStability()}} — the TDS engine over a multivariate series.
\item \code{\link[=tdsSurrogateThreshold]{tdsSurrogateThreshold()}} — surrogate-based significance threshold.
\item \code{\link[=tdsNetwork]{tdsNetwork()}} — build a thresholded organ-interaction network.
\item \code{\link[=tdsNetworkByState]{tdsNetworkByState()}} — state-resolved networks + reconfiguration.
\item \code{\link[=physioNodeMatrix]{physioNodeMatrix()}} — assemble a node matrix of physiological systems.
}
}
